{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "cases": [
        {
            "id": "list-reflow",
            "file": "lists.md",
            "languageId": "markdown",
            "snapshot": {
                "version": 1,
                "providerId": "deterministic-replay",
                "sourceLanguage": "en",
                "targetLanguage": "zh-CN"
            },
            "response": {
                "version": 1,
                "text": "1. 围绕主要任务组织页面，每个主要区域都应承担明确的职责。\n\n2. 在滚动页面的首屏展示主题、决策或主要工作区域。\n   让实际主题成为首屏的视觉重点。\n\n3. 每张幻灯片清楚表达一个核心观点，并在同页给出依据。\n\n4. 根据标题的作用和容器调整字号，操作区域使用紧凑的标题。\n\n5. 将说明放在对应的图像、控件或观点附近，避免读者来回对照。\n\n6. 在首屏展示下一节的部分内容，让读者知道页面仍可向下滚动。\n\n7. 优先采用有力的整体构图，减少可相互替换的通栏和重复卡片。"
            },
            "expect": {
                "status": "translated",
                "units": [
                    {
                        "id": "item-1",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 0,
                            "end": 129
                        },
                        "source": "1. Organize the page around the primary task, not around a catalog of available content. Every major region needs a distinct job.",
                        "translation": "1. 围绕主要任务组织页面，每个主要区域都应承担明确的职责。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-2",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 130,
                            "end": 377
                        },
                        "source": "2. On scrolling pages, put the subject, decision, or primary working surface in the first viewport. On product, venue, portfolio, or object-focused pages, make the actual subject a strong first-viewport signal rather than a small navigation label.",
                        "translation": "2. 在滚动页面的首屏展示主题、决策或主要工作区域。\n   让实际主题成为首屏的视觉重点。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-3",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 378,
                            "end": 508
                        },
                        "source": "3. On a presentation slide, make one core claim or idea readable at presentation distance and keep its evidence on the same slide.",
                        "translation": "3. 每张幻灯片清楚表达一个核心观点，并在同页给出依据。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-4",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 509,
                            "end": 670
                        },
                        "source": "4. Size headings to their role and container. Reserve display-scale type for a genuine page-level introduction; use compact headings inside operational surfaces.",
                        "translation": "4. 根据标题的作用和容器调整字号，操作区域使用紧凑的标题。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-5",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 671,
                            "end": 816
                        },
                        "source": "5. Keep supporting copy close to the visual, control, or claim it explains. Do not make users reconcile distant labels, legends, and conclusions.",
                        "translation": "5. 将说明放在对应的图像、控件或观点附近，避免读者来回对照。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-6",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 817,
                            "end": 966
                        },
                        "source": "6. On scrolling pages, show a hint of the next meaningful section below a first-screen introduction so the page does not appear finished at the fold.",
                        "translation": "6. 在首屏展示下一节的部分内容，让读者知道页面仍可向下滚动。"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "item-7",
                        "range": {
                            "start": 967,
                            "end": 1070
                        },
                        "source": "7. Prefer one strong composition over a sequence of interchangeable full-width bands or repeated cards.",
                        "translation": "7. 优先采用有力的整体构图，减少可相互替换的通栏和重复卡片。"
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
